467 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 224 0 R
/T (this document explains every decision in the mini marketplace ERD and why we made it. the marketplace follows the Daraz model: one user can both buy and sell, one cart holds items from many sellers, and each seller ships their own parcel through Leopards Courier. customers pay online \(card or wallet\) or cash on delivery.)
/E (this document explains every decision in the mini marketplace ERD and why we made it. the marketplace follows the Daraz model: one user can both buy and sell, one cart holds items from many sellers, and each seller ships their own parcel through Leopards Courier. customers pay online \(card or wallet\) or cash on delivery.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
468 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 224 0 R
/T (the ERD has 12 tables grouped into 6 areas. table names are written in quotations and columns in code formatting.)
/E (the ERD has 12 tables grouped into 6 areas. table names are written in quotations and columns in code formatting.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
469 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 224 0 R
/T (three rules apply across every table:)
/E (three rules apply across every table:)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
470 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 224 0 R
/T (money is stored in paisa as whole numbers. price, total, amount and every other money column is an integer, so Rs 1,299 is stored as 129900. the column names don't mention paisa, so this rule is where the unit is defined. floats can't represent most decimal amounts exactly and rounding errors pile up over thousands of orders. anything an order depends on is copied at checkout. product name, options, unit price, commission rate and shipping address are copied \(snapshotted\) onto the order. a seller editing a product or a customer editing an address later never changes an order that already happened.)
/E (money is stored in paisa as whole numbers. price, total, amount and every other money column is an integer, so Rs 1,299 is stored as 129900. the column names don't mention paisa, so this rule is where the unit is defined. floats can't represent most decimal amounts exactly and rounding errors pile up over thousands of orders. anything an order depends on is copied at checkout. product name, options, unit price, commission rate and shipping address are copied \(snapshotted\) onto the order. a seller editing a product or a customer editing an address later never changes an order that already happened.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
471 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 224 0 R
/T (fixed sets of values are enums. statuses, methods and types are enums so the database itself rejects a value we never planned for.)
/E (fixed sets of values are enums. statuses, methods and types are enums so the database itself rejects a value we never planned for.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
